are released into a wild environment. Our results clearly show that captivity has altered the giant panda microbiome, which could have unintended negative consequences on their adaptability and the ecosystem during the reintroduction of giant pandas into the wild."	2019.0	Genes	YES		METAGENOMIC	YES	Viridiplantae	Streptophyta	Malpighiales	Pandaceae		Panda	10.3390/genes10100827				WGA:196; WGS:11	11	0			gut metagenome	feces	Metagenome or environmental sample from gut metagenome	207.0	https://doi.org/10.3390/genes10100827	True	True	Panda	True	giant panda	True	giant panda	False		False	ENA + paper	Fecal samples were sequenced from wild and captive giant pandas using 16S rRNA and shotgun metagenomics.	DIVERSE	207	METAGENOMIC:207	207
